# Godot 4 GDScript

Use Godot 4 syntax only. Replace Godot 3 patterns:

| Godot 3 | Godot 4 |
|---|---|
| `export var speed = 10` | `@export var speed: float = 10.0` |
| `onready var x = $X` | `@onready var x: Node = $X` |
| `yield(obj, "sig")` | `await obj.sig` |
| `connect("pressed", self, "_on_pressed")` | `pressed.connect(_on_pressed)` |
| `emit_signal("died")` | `died.emit()` |
| `KinematicBody2D` | `CharacterBody2D` |
| `move_and_slide(velocity, Vector2.UP)` | set `velocity`, then `move_and_slide()` |
| `scene.instance()` | `scene.instantiate()` |
| `tool` | `@tool` |
| `setget` | `var x: int: set = _set_x, get = _get_x` |

- Use static typing everywhere: `var hp: int = 3`, `func hit(dmg: int) -> void:`.
- Declare signals with types: `signal health_changed(new_value: int)`.
- "Call down, signal up": parents call child methods; children emit signals. Don't use `get_parent()` chains.
- Use `@export` node references or `%UniqueName` instead of long `$A/B/C` paths.
- Use autoloads sparingly, for truly global state (settings, save game, event bus).
- Physics/movement in `_physics_process(delta)`; per-frame visuals in `_process(delta)`.
- Don't edit `.tscn` / `.tres` files by hand unless asked; describe the editor change instead.
